105
00:10:06.174 --> 00:10:09.134
- Here you go.
- Yo. Mikey. toss me a ninja slice!

106
00:10:09.213 --> 00:10:11.175
Donny. Statue of Liberty!

107
00:10:11.214 --> 00:10:14.174
- Come on. throw it! Over here!
- Mike. no!

108
00:10:14.255 --> 00:10:17.335
i'm right here! He's at the forty!
He's at the twenty!

109
00:10:17.416 --> 00:10:21.174
He looks. He rolls back.
He goes deep.

110
00:10:21.255 --> 00:10:23.055
- Yeah!
- Donatello. stop!

111
00:10:24.015 --> 00:10:26.016
Touchdown!
Yeah!

112
00:10:26.094 --> 00:10:29.015
- Yeah!
- Yeah!

113
00:10:29.094 --> 00:10:32.335
So. any luck finding
a new place to live yet?

114
00:10:32.414 --> 00:10:35.495
Well. you know. in this market
it's actually very difficult...

115
00:10:35.536 --> 00:10:37.935
to find good
subterranean housing.

116
00:10:37.974 --> 00:10:40.815
Hey. we could always go back
to the old sewer den.

117
00:10:40.896 --> 00:10:44.495
- Well...
- Right. Raph. It's a little tough...

118
00:10:44.575 --> 00:10:47.176
when about 500 members
of the Foot Clan...

119
00:10:47.215 --> 00:10:49.735
- Know where you live.
- He's right.

120
00:10:49.816 --> 00:10:51.856
We kicked their butts.
They're all in jail.

121
00:10:51.935 --> 00:10:54.097
'Sides. we took out
the Shredder...

122
00:10:54.137 --> 00:10:55.935
so what's everybody
so worried about?

123
00:10:56.016 --> 00:10:57.376
He's right.

124
00:10:57.455 --> 00:10:59.816
No. Splinter took out
the Shredder.

125
00:10:59.895 --> 00:11:02.296
- They're both right.
- Yeah. yeah.

126
00:11:02.376 --> 00:11:04.656
i was there. Leo.
Remember?

127
00:11:04.695 --> 00:11:08.616
Old Shred did a swan dive
with a half gainer...

128
00:11:08.656 --> 00:11:10.737
right into the back
of a garbage truck!

129
00:11:13.615 --> 00:11:15.135
Come away from there!

130
00:11:15.217 --> 00:11:17.497
Geez. i was just...

131
00:11:17.575 --> 00:11:19.416
Never forget
who you are.

132
00:11:19.497 --> 00:11:24.697
You are ninja. You must always
practice the art of invisibility.

133
00:11:24.776 --> 00:11:28.017
- All of you.
- Well. i don't get it.

134
00:11:28.058 --> 00:11:34.177
i mean. why? We saved the city.
Why can't we just go out and...

135
00:11:34.256 --> 00:11:37.018
Stand before me. my sons.

136
00:11:43.497 --> 00:11:48.138
For 15 years.
you have been confined below.

137
00:11:48.178 --> 00:11:53.897
Now the outside world
beckons your teenage minds...

138
00:11:53.938 --> 00:11:56.778
but they could
never understand.

139
00:11:56.818 --> 00:12:00.298
Their world
can never be ours.

140
00:12:02.618 --> 00:12:04.858
Not even pizza?

141
00:12:08.337 --> 00:12:09.497
Pizza's okay.

142
00:12:10.738 --> 00:12:12.858
Man. you give a guy
a heart attack.

143
00:12:14.218 --> 00:12:16.258
Here. let me get
you guys some napkins.

144
00:12:16.338 --> 00:12:18.098
- What for?
- What for?

145
00:12:21.739 --> 00:12:25.660
Take heart. child.
We will not be here much longer.

146
00:12:25.739 --> 00:12:29.098
Oh. no. no. You guys can
stay here as long as you want.

147
00:12:29.138 --> 00:12:31.298
- Oh. gee. Thanks a lot.
- No!

148
00:12:31.378 --> 00:12:35.060
- We do not belong here above.
- Oh. man!

149
00:12:35.099 --> 00:12:36.977
Yes. Master Splinter.

150
00:12:40.219 --> 00:12:43.901
Hey! Ten flips now!

151
00:12:43.980 --> 00:12:45.619
Go!

152
00:12:45.659 --> 00:12:47.859
Kids.

153
00:12:49.738 --> 00:12:52.339
- One.
- One.

154
00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:54.378
Such energy is wasted.

155
00:12:54.460 --> 00:12:56.579
- Two.
- Remember...

156
00:12:56.659 --> 00:13:00.940
the true ninja is
a master of all things...

157
00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:03.498
a master of his environment...

158
00:13:03.539 --> 00:13:06.299
a master of himself.

159
00:13:06.379 --> 00:13:10.061
Focus your thoughts
on where we must go...

160
00:13:10.100 --> 00:13:13.739
and leave the Shredder buried.

161
00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:21.180
Let's go!

162
00:14:05.021 --> 00:14:06.942
Come on.

163
00:14:12.022 --> 00:14:13.862
is this it?

164
00:14:13.942 --> 00:14:16.102
Everyone else must've
been picked up.

165
00:14:17.021 --> 00:14:18.902
Well. maybe they
didn't find us.

166
00:14:18.942 --> 00:14:22.782
Hey. we all knew the junkyard
was our fallback spot.

167
00:14:25.821 --> 00:14:29.143
Our father gone!

168
00:14:30.142 --> 00:14:32.061
They will pay!

169
00:14:34.581 --> 00:14:38.022
i. Tatsu. now lead.

170
00:14:38.102 --> 00:14:41.423
Let any who challenge
step forward.

171
00:14:43.544 --> 00:14:45.261
i challenge.

172
00:14:49.903 --> 00:14:51.343
His face!

173
00:14:52.343 --> 00:14:55.903
Master Shredder!

174
00:14:59.463 --> 00:15:02.582
Choose the best man
from those that remain...

175
00:15:02.621 --> 00:15:04.743
to follow the reporter.

176
00:15:04.823 --> 00:15:09.744
She is the key to finding
the creatures that did this to me.

177
00:15:09.823 --> 00:15:11.104
Yes. Master.

178
00:15:11.182 --> 00:15:13.743
Next. Master.
we rebuild the Foot?

179
00:15:15.863 --> 00:15:19.545
There is only
one thing next.

180
00:15:19.584 --> 00:15:21.943
Revenge.

181
00:15:22.023 --> 00:15:24.345
And in this day and age
of ecological abuse...

182
00:15:24.383 --> 00:15:27.424
it's nice to find a company
that's doing something to help.

183
00:15:27.505 --> 00:15:30.063
joining me on the final day
of their cleanup efforts...

184
00:15:30.144 --> 00:15:33.425
is Techno Global Research
industries spokesman...

185
00:15:33.464 --> 00:15:35.864
Professorjordan Perry.

186
00:15:35.905 --> 00:15:37.985
Excuse me. Professor?

187
00:15:39.343 --> 00:15:42.544
- Good afternoon.
- Good afternoon. Miss O'Neil.

188
00:15:42.585 --> 00:15:44.824
Professor.
perhaps you can tell us...

189
00:15:44.904 --> 00:15:48.064
why TGRi has finally decided
to clean up the waste...

190
00:15:48.144 --> 00:15:49.984
that's been burying here for years.

191
00:15:50.064 --> 00:15:51.905
Would you like me
to keep my answer succinct...

192
00:15:51.984 --> 00:15:54.423
or will you be able to edit later on
in case i start to ramble...

193
00:15:54.504 --> 00:15:58.585
- Which i'm in the habit of doing.
- Professor. we're live.

194
00:16:00.145 --> 00:16:01.665
Oh. right. well. yes.

195
00:16:01.744 --> 00:16:04.425
Our organization has always
been very concerned...

196
00:16:04.505 --> 00:16:06.744
with the welfare
of the community we serve.

197
00:16:06.824 --> 00:16:09.985
- Indeed. TGRI is...
- Man. who is this spasmatic?

198
00:16:10.865 --> 00:16:13.744
Would you give the guy a break?
He's a scientist.

199
00:16:13.785 --> 00:16:16.945
Yeah. fascinating.
Hey. isn't Oprah on?

200
00:16:16.985 --> 00:16:21.745
Raph. just leave it.
We're watching April.

201
00:16:28.706 --> 00:16:32.626
And dispose of them
in an ecologically more suitable way.

202
00:16:32.706 --> 00:16:35.745
Hey. Mikey. do you think
you can crunch any louder?

203
00:16:35.825 --> 00:16:38.025
i can still hear
out of this one.

204
00:16:46.066 --> 00:16:48.826
Come on.
let's change this.

205
00:16:48.866 --> 00:16:52.385
Hey. maybe somebody's got something
on our fight last night.

206
00:16:53.347 --> 00:16:55.226
Do not change channel.

207
00:16:55.306 --> 00:16:57.106
Reporting live from
Bayonne. NewJersey...

208
00:16:57.146 --> 00:16:59.666
this is April O'Neil.
Channel Three News.

209
00:16:59.707 --> 00:17:01.706
- Back to you.
- And that's it. We're off.

210
00:17:01.785 --> 00:17:04.465
Great.
Thank you.

211
00:17:04.506 --> 00:17:08.107
Professor. would you mind if i asked you
a few follow-up questions?

212
00:17:08.188 --> 00:17:10.226
Not at all. Oh. drat!

213
00:17:10.306 --> 00:17:12.185
You know. we're gonna
have to do it another time.

214
00:17:12.226 --> 00:17:14.427
it's been a great pleasure
meeting you. Miss O'Neil.

215
00:17:14.507 --> 00:17:17.427
All press members
must now clear the area.

216
00:17:17.507 --> 00:17:22.746
Okay. great.
Report back at 3:00. okay?

217
00:17:22.827 --> 00:17:25.467
- Enjoying your first day. Freddy?
- Yeah.

218
00:17:25.547 --> 00:17:27.387
Hey. what were you
going to ask him?

219
00:17:27.467 --> 00:17:30.347
Well. i don't know.

220
00:17:30.426 --> 00:17:33.267
Don't worry about it.
i'm paid to be suspicious.

221
00:17:34.948 --> 00:17:37.269
- Come on. come on.
- Oh. yeah. Sorry.

222
00:17:39.708 --> 00:17:43.988
All non-TGRI employees
must now vacate the area.

223
00:17:45.308 --> 00:17:47.187
Right here.

224
00:17:49.788 --> 00:17:52.269
How could you
have missed this?

225
00:17:52.348 --> 00:17:54.188
i don't know.

226
00:17:54.269 --> 00:17:56.748
Grab some men.
i'll go find the professor.

227
00:17:56.828 --> 00:17:59.188
We've got to
take care of this now.

228
00:17:59.268 --> 00:18:01.148
- Go.
- Right.

229
00:18:03.389 --> 00:18:07.028
All members of the press must
return their visitor badges...

230
00:18:07.067 --> 00:18:09.028
at the main gate.

231
00:18:23.429 --> 00:18:25.309
Dandelions?

232
00:18:35.949 --> 00:18:38.029
Now. if the soil is
contaminated so far away...

233
00:18:38.110 --> 00:18:40.110
there must be more leaky
canisters than we thought.

234
00:18:40.189 --> 00:18:42.110
But how could that be?
They were only buried 15 years ago.

235
00:18:42.188 --> 00:18:46.509
Fifteen. fifty. Just make sure
the rest are found and removed.

236
00:18:46.590 --> 00:18:48.750
Maybe it wasn't such a good idea
to invite the press.

237
00:18:48.830 --> 00:18:51.950
Sometimes the best way to hide
is right out in public.

238
00:18:52.031 --> 00:18:54.991
if any of it fell
into the wrong hands...

239
00:18:55.069 --> 00:18:57.150
i'm well aware of the risks.

240
00:18:57.230 --> 00:19:00.150
Containment team. sector three.

241
00:19:03.830 --> 00:19:07.192
This is not the reason
i sent you to follow her.

242
00:19:07.231 --> 00:19:10.830
- No. Master. but i thought...
- Silence!

243
00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.871
This may be even better.

244
00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:19.670
Whatever caused this mutation
may be useful against my enemies.

245
00:19:20.951 --> 00:19:23.871
Tatsu. gather your best men.

246
00:19:23.951 --> 00:19:26.392
You have a mission tonight.

247
00:19:49.792 --> 00:19:51.952
Hey. guys!
Check this!

248
00:19:52.032 --> 00:19:54.512
Wax on. Wax off.

249
00:19:54.593 --> 00:19:57.593
- Wax on...
- Mouth off!

250
00:19:57.632 --> 00:20:00.191
- Hey. everyone's a critic.
- Hello?

251
00:20:00.271 --> 00:20:02.432
Oh. man!

252
00:20:02.513 --> 00:20:05.992
- April. you spoiled our surprise.
- We were gonna clean everything up.

253
00:20:06.071 --> 00:20:09.231
Thanks. guys.
Where's Splinter?

254
00:20:09.953 --> 00:20:12.913
He's been up on the roof
ever since he saw your report.

255
00:20:13.911 --> 00:20:16.111
Really? Doing what?

256
00:20:16.192 --> 00:20:19.512
Coming to a decision.

257
00:20:20.673 --> 00:20:23.553
You've been meditating many hours.
Master Splinter.

258
00:20:23.632 --> 00:20:27.752
Yes. and it is time.
join me above.

259
00:20:28.953 --> 00:20:31.353
Maybe you better hear
what he has to say.

260
00:20:31.434 --> 00:20:35.431
These last hours
have been spent...

261
00:20:35.512 --> 00:20:38.954
pondering many questions.

262
00:20:39.033 --> 00:20:44.313
Some are the very questions
of our origin.

263
00:20:44.393 --> 00:20:45.753
The sewer.

264
00:20:45.793 --> 00:20:48.393
Our transformation.

265
00:20:48.473 --> 00:20:51.553
But the answers have
always remained...

266
00:20:51.633 --> 00:20:54.273
hidden in the past...

267
00:20:54.354 --> 00:20:58.714
veiled by a shadow
too deep to penetrate...

268
00:21:00.193 --> 00:21:01.473
until now.

269
00:21:04.354 --> 00:21:06.633
A light from the present...

270
00:21:06.714 --> 00:21:11.234
reaches back
to illuminate that shadow.

271
00:21:11.313 --> 00:21:15.395
You have never seen this.
but know what it is.

272
00:21:16.074 --> 00:21:20.834
- That's the canister that had the ooze!
- That transformed us all.

273
00:21:20.874 --> 00:21:24.675
i have kept it these 15 years.

274
00:21:24.715 --> 00:21:28.194
But why do you only show us
now. Master Splinter?

275
00:21:31.594 --> 00:21:33.595
TGRi!

276
00:21:33.675 --> 00:21:36.554
The interview today.
i knew it!

277
00:21:36.633 --> 00:21:39.514
i knew that there was something else
going on with those guys.

278
00:21:39.595 --> 00:21:42.955
Yes. and we must know what...

279
00:21:43.035 --> 00:21:46.874
for if the contents of this
canister were not unique...

280
00:21:46.914 --> 00:21:51.476
the city may now face
grave danger.

281
00:21:51.554 --> 00:21:54.235
After all these years.

282
00:21:54.275 --> 00:21:57.155
After all this time
wondering who we are.

283
00:21:57.195 --> 00:22:01.516
The past returns. my son.

284
00:22:03.356 --> 00:22:08.555
it is time to seek our answers.

285
00:22:41.076 --> 00:22:42.997
Disposed.

286
00:22:47.997 --> 00:22:50.876
Well. you're the last one.
aren't you?

287
00:22:56.757 --> 00:22:59.358
- Come on guys.
- I love this spy stuff.

288
00:22:59.396 --> 00:23:01.276
Yeah.

289
00:23:05.439 --> 00:23:07.278
Not much to this place.

290
00:23:09.157 --> 00:23:11.037
it doesn't look like
there's any night security...

291
00:23:11.117 --> 00:23:13.118
but we better
move in quiet.

292
00:23:13.198 --> 00:23:15.397
- Yeah.
- Come on. Leo.

293
00:23:15.478 --> 00:23:19.398
What do you say?
Let's do it. eh?

294
00:23:19.478 --> 00:23:22.198
- Let's do it!
- Let's do it!

295
00:23:23.559 --> 00:23:25.917
- Times Square city!
- I don't believe it!

296
00:23:25.997 --> 00:23:29.438
- Like video games in 3-D!
- Totally massive!

297
00:23:30.678 --> 00:23:33.359
Would you get a load
of this crazy joint!

298
00:23:33.438 --> 00:23:37.197
The past returns. I knew
we'd find something special.

299
00:23:37.277 --> 00:23:39.718
i'll say special.
Look at this.

300
00:23:39.799 --> 00:23:43.959
- Hey. where do you put the quarter?
- Will you stop messing around?

301
00:23:44.038 --> 00:23:46.239
Hey. guys. over there!

302
00:23:53.558 --> 00:23:56.238
- What do you make of it. Donny?
- Well. i'm not sure.

303
00:23:56.318 --> 00:23:58.158
Looks like just a bunch
of serial numbers.

304
00:23:58.239 --> 00:23:59.958
Let's see. uh...

305
00:24:00.038 --> 00:24:02.878
Disposed.
Disposed.

306
00:24:03.839 --> 00:24:07.200
- Disposed.
- Hey. dudes. we're too late.

307
00:24:07.278 --> 00:24:09.759
Like. uh. no deposit.
no return.

308
00:24:09.800 --> 00:24:12.319
Well. except maybe this one.

309
00:24:12.398 --> 00:24:14.399
What do you mean?

310
00:24:14.439 --> 00:24:15.600
Look!

311
00:24:16.878 --> 00:24:17.799
"Active."

312
00:24:17.839 --> 00:24:19.919
- Yeah.
- Can you bring up the file?

313
00:24:19.999 --> 00:24:22.679
Well. i could try.

314
00:24:22.758 --> 00:24:26.239
But if the database is coded.
the whole system might go down.

315
00:24:28.121 --> 00:24:30.519
- Do it!
- Yeah. yeah!

316
00:24:42.279 --> 00:24:43.680
- Drag.
- Drat.

317
00:24:43.760 --> 00:24:46.840
No. no. no! So close!

318
00:24:50.280 --> 00:24:53.279
- What?
- The Foot!

319
00:24:55.722 --> 00:24:57.401
He's got the canister!

320
00:24:57.480 --> 00:24:59.761
- Get it!
- I got him!

321
00:25:17.361 --> 00:25:18.322
Go. go. go. go!

322
00:25:37.921 --> 00:25:40.562
- Throw it over here.
- Go long! Go long!

323
00:25:40.642 --> 00:25:43.083
Down field!
Turtle in the open!

324
00:25:47.282 --> 00:25:49.882
Ah. one. two. three. punt!

325
00:25:55.881 --> 00:25:58.603
Hey. guys. huddle.
Come here. Come on.

326
00:25:58.642 --> 00:26:01.482
Mikey. you go up the middle.
You guys take the sides.

327
00:26:01.523 --> 00:26:04.683
- Got it.
- I don't get it.

328
00:26:04.761 --> 00:26:05.883
Ready. break!

329
00:26:28.163 --> 00:26:30.843
Hey. Mikey. surf's up. dude!

330
00:26:33.763 --> 00:26:35.564
Wipe out!

331
00:26:38.803 --> 00:26:40.803
Ninja vanish!

332
00:26:48.204 --> 00:26:50.124
Oh. great!

333
00:26:51.883 --> 00:26:54.123
Terrific!

334
00:26:56.085 --> 00:26:58.004
Wonderful!

335
00:27:02.005 --> 00:27:03.925
Bummer!

336
00:27:06.604 --> 00:27:10.524
And this was the only one?

337
00:27:10.604 --> 00:27:12.804
Then it's time to
find out exactly...

338
00:27:12.845 --> 00:27:16.804
what this ooze can do.

339
00:27:16.885 --> 00:27:19.764
isn't it. Professor?

340
00:27:21.884 --> 00:27:24.845
We'll find a home soon. Paulina.
and then it'll be just you and me.

341
00:27:24.924 --> 00:27:28.165
Now. look. we've all talked about it.
We've decided to do it...

342
00:27:28.204 --> 00:27:31.005
- And that's all there is to it.
- But i don't understand.

343
00:27:31.086 --> 00:27:33.524
You guys haven't even found
a new place to live yet.

344
00:27:33.604 --> 00:27:37.725
it's too dangerous to stay here with you
when the Foot are out there. They might be
looking for us.

345
00:27:39.725 --> 00:27:42.405
We could go looking for them
for a change.

346
00:27:42.445 --> 00:27:44.405
i mean. they've got the ooze.

347
00:27:44.485 --> 00:27:48.006
- First we move. then we look.
- I don't know about you guys...

348
00:27:48.087 --> 00:27:51.685
- But i could really go for a slice of...
- Pizza!

349
00:27:51.725 --> 00:27:53.125
Whoa! Spookular!

350
00:27:53.165 --> 00:27:55.366
Miss O'Neil?

351
00:27:58.246 --> 00:28:02.086
Wait! I'll be right there.

352
00:28:07.125 --> 00:28:10.846
- What?
- I didn't order any pizza.

353
00:28:10.926 --> 00:28:14.046
Oh. i know.
But the guy in 313 did...

354
00:28:14.126 --> 00:28:16.486
and now he doesn't
seem to be there.

355
00:28:17.606 --> 00:28:19.927
i figured since you
order so much anyway...

356
00:28:20.006 --> 00:28:22.446
that. you know. maybe you...

357
00:28:24.286 --> 00:28:27.086
- Where'd these come from?
- Those...

358
00:28:27.167 --> 00:28:28.766
are mine!

359
00:28:28.846 --> 00:28:30.806
Yeah. I...

360
00:28:30.886 --> 00:28:34.726
i like to do a little chucking
every now and then.

361
00:28:39.767 --> 00:28:42.807
Yeah.
i'd keep practicing.

362
00:28:42.888 --> 00:28:46.168
On second thought.
why don't i take this pizza anyway?

363
00:28:46.248 --> 00:28:49.008
i can always use more.
Let me get my wallet.

364
00:28:49.047 --> 00:28:50.447
No. that's okay.

365
00:28:50.488 --> 00:28:52.367
- Yes. please.
- Don't worry about it.

366
00:28:52.407 --> 00:28:54.887
One last thing. though.
You might want to know about this!

367
00:28:56.367 --> 00:28:58.767
- You guys!
- What's the big idea?

368
00:28:58.807 --> 00:29:02.248
Can i hurt him? Please!
Tell me i can hurt him!

369
00:29:02.327 --> 00:29:04.369
- Please. please!
- Take it easy.

370
00:29:08.008 --> 00:29:11.608
i think you'd better sit down.

371
00:29:19.087 --> 00:29:22.689
And with an old
Renaissance art book...

372
00:29:22.769 --> 00:29:25.489
i found in a storm drain...

373
00:29:25.568 --> 00:29:27.889
i gave them all names.

374
00:29:27.968 --> 00:29:29.968
Yeah.

375
00:29:30.049 --> 00:29:33.488
i'm Leonardo.

376
00:29:33.569 --> 00:29:35.569
i'm Michaelangelo.

377
00:29:37.049 --> 00:29:38.929
Donatello.

378
00:29:38.968 --> 00:29:40.849
i'm Rafael.

379
00:29:40.889 --> 00:29:43.528
Yeah. all the good ones
end in "O."

380
00:29:45.569 --> 00:29:47.649
- Michaelangelo!
- Yeah?

381
00:29:47.728 --> 00:29:50.689
- Go!
- All right.

382
00:29:50.767 --> 00:29:53.969
i can't believe
every time i...

383
00:29:56.050 --> 00:29:57.370
One.

384
00:29:59.570 --> 00:30:01.888
- Two.
- Basically. what you're telling me...

385
00:30:01.969 --> 00:30:04.889
is you guys were all slimed!

386
00:30:05.729 --> 00:30:10.088
it wasn't slime. It was ooze.
And there's more of it out there.

387
00:30:10.169 --> 00:30:12.409
- Where?
- We're not sure.

388
00:30:12.489 --> 00:30:15.130
See. there's this sort of
clan of ninja thieves.

389
00:30:15.209 --> 00:30:17.411
- A secret group. They call themselves...
- The Foot?

390
00:30:17.491 --> 00:30:19.930
- You've heard of'em?
- The word is out...

391
00:30:20.008 --> 00:30:22.930
that these guys are looking
for anybody they can find...

392
00:30:23.010 --> 00:30:25.931
with martial arts talent.
especially teenagers.

393
00:30:26.890 --> 00:30:32.490
Hey. and if i let myself get recruited.
guess what that might lead us to?

394
00:30:32.530 --> 00:30:34.652
No way. Keno.

395
00:30:34.730 --> 00:30:36.889
Forget about it.

396
00:30:36.970 --> 00:30:40.490
Believe me. i really hate to say this.
but the kid's got a...

397
00:30:40.531 --> 00:30:42.932
- No!
- Why not?

398
00:30:43.010 --> 00:30:45.930
Too dangerous.

399
00:30:46.010 --> 00:30:47.410
But i thought we...

400
00:30:49.651 --> 00:30:50.571
Oh. man.

401
00:30:50.611 --> 00:30:53.131
Twenty.

402
00:30:53.211 --> 00:30:56.091
Twenty-one.
Twenty...

403
00:31:00.371 --> 00:31:02.412
One? Yeah.

404
00:31:09.090 --> 00:31:12.452
And these are the two most vicious
animals you could find?

405
00:31:13.491 --> 00:31:15.372
Good.

406
00:31:15.412 --> 00:31:18.011
- Professor?
- Preparations are complete. however...

407
00:31:18.092 --> 00:31:21.211
- Begin!
- I must re-register my protest...

408
00:31:21.291 --> 00:31:23.332
and remind you
of the immense danger if...

409
00:31:26.692 --> 00:31:29.812
That's enough talk from me.
We'll begin.

410
00:32:00.093 --> 00:32:02.573
Yes.

411
00:32:08.573 --> 00:32:11.053
- Clear.
- Go. go. Move.

412
00:32:18.174 --> 00:32:20.093
- See ya. April.
- Bye.

413
00:32:22.694 --> 00:32:23.853
Wish us luck.

414
00:32:28.493 --> 00:32:30.414
We'll be back for Splinter.

415
00:32:32.334 --> 00:32:36.053
The lives of two people don't amount
to a hill of beans in this crazy world.

416
00:32:36.093 --> 00:32:37.974
That's why you're
gettin' on that plane.

417
00:32:38.014 --> 00:32:40.294
- Maybe not today. maybe not to...
- Would you stop!

418
00:32:41.455 --> 00:32:42.735
See ya.

419
00:32:59.775 --> 00:33:02.815
All right. hold it.
This is stupid.

420
00:33:02.896 --> 00:33:04.814
We got the Foot up there
with the ooze...

421
00:33:04.855 --> 00:33:07.215
and we're down here
playing "Century 21."

422
00:33:07.255 --> 00:33:09.455
- Raph!
- Come on. Leo.

423
00:33:09.495 --> 00:33:12.015
Even you could think of something
better to do than this.

424
00:33:12.056 --> 00:33:14.935
i already have.
Now. let's get going!

425
00:33:15.015 --> 00:33:17.215
That's it.
i'm goin' up.

426
00:33:17.815 --> 00:33:21.136
- No. you're not!
- Let go of my arm. Leo.

427
00:33:21.176 --> 00:33:24.894
Guys. guys. guys!
i just got an idea.

428
00:33:24.975 --> 00:33:27.855
Two words that could solve
all our housing problems.

429
00:33:27.935 --> 00:33:31.095
Time share!

430
00:33:31.136 --> 00:33:34.015
- Not quite ripe yet.
- I'm outta here.

431
00:33:34.096 --> 00:33:36.655
But... Oh. man!

432
00:33:37.496 --> 00:33:39.855
Oh. boy.

433
00:33:41.135 --> 00:33:43.015
- Come on.
- Yeah.

434
00:33:43.095 --> 00:33:47.776
- Finding a home should be easy.
- But no!

435
00:33:47.856 --> 00:33:50.016
You'd think even an idiot
could find a place down here.

436
00:33:50.096 --> 00:33:51.537
But no...

437
00:33:53.616 --> 00:33:56.017
Oh. no!
Mikey. buddy!

438
00:33:56.096 --> 00:33:59.177
- Mikey. are you okay?
- Mikey!

439
00:33:59.255 --> 00:34:02.096
Check it out!

440
00:34:02.137 --> 00:34:03.457
Yeah!

441
00:34:03.537 --> 00:34:07.335
- Whoa!
- Okay. bro? Come on. Leo!

442
00:34:08.856 --> 00:34:10.856
- You all right?
- No prob.

443
00:34:19.416 --> 00:34:22.418
Power! Yeah.

444
00:34:25.457 --> 00:34:27.778
Oh. yeah!

445
00:34:29.897 --> 00:34:32.378
Look. I don't believe this.

446
00:34:34.378 --> 00:34:37.777
- Yes!
- Yes. yes!

447
00:34:40.697 --> 00:34:43.017
it's like spider city!

448
00:34:43.098 --> 00:34:45.098
Great!

449
00:34:45.177 --> 00:34:47.817
Rock-a-bye-baby.

450
00:34:47.898 --> 00:34:49.738
it's roomy!

451
00:34:49.818 --> 00:34:52.177
And it's well hidden. huh?

452
00:34:52.258 --> 00:34:54.178
So what do ya think?

453
00:34:55.738 --> 00:34:59.657
You know. i hear the sewers
in Connecticut are really nice.

454
00:34:59.738 --> 00:35:01.939
- Yeah. Come on.
- This is great!

455
00:35:07.579 --> 00:35:11.538
- How much longer?
- Look. i told you. i don't know.

456
00:35:11.618 --> 00:35:13.659
it takes time. Days!

457
00:35:13.738 --> 00:35:16.659
i want them
as soon as possible.

458
00:35:16.699 --> 00:35:19.579
- I told...
- Sit down!

459
00:35:19.658 --> 00:35:22.578
Aren't these enough
for your vengeance?

460
00:35:22.658 --> 00:35:25.778
The Foot have already
failed against them.

461
00:35:25.820 --> 00:35:28.020
i have failed.

462
00:35:29.898 --> 00:35:33.899
But the next time
will be different.

463
00:35:33.980 --> 00:35:38.420
The next fight will be
freak against freak!

464
00:35:42.860 --> 00:35:46.420
April. will you listen
just for a minute?

465
00:35:46.460 --> 00:35:48.339
it's a ratings week!

466
00:35:48.379 --> 00:35:51.699
Phil. i told you.
i am following up on TGRi.

467
00:35:51.780 --> 00:35:54.100
There's more going on there
than we know.

468
00:35:54.139 --> 00:35:57.618
Look. that story is over.
We need something solid.

469
00:35:57.699 --> 00:36:01.940
Something fresh.
i mean. like... like this.

470
00:36:01.979 --> 00:36:05.140
- She's busy right now.
- "Looking ahead.

471
00:36:05.181 --> 00:36:07.580
- Swimsuits in the '90s"?
- My interest is peaked.

472
00:36:07.620 --> 00:36:10.421
Phil. i gotta get going.

473
00:36:10.461 --> 00:36:12.459
You are always so busy.

474
00:36:12.540 --> 00:36:15.261
i'm the news manager here. April!

475
00:36:15.300 --> 00:36:18.100
April. there's a call for you.

476
00:36:19.501 --> 00:36:21.300
Tell them i'll call them back.

477
00:36:21.341 --> 00:36:24.700
He sounds pretty insistent.
Says his name's Donny.

478
00:36:24.780 --> 00:36:28.340
Listen. tell Donny that she's busy
with her news manager right now...

479
00:36:28.380 --> 00:36:29.900
and that she can't...

480
00:36:33.861 --> 00:36:37.100
Where are you guys?
Did you find a place to live yet?

481
00:36:37.181 --> 00:36:39.342
Oh. yeah. but i...

482
00:36:40.541 --> 00:36:43.380
it's not much right now.
but we'll bring you down.

483
00:36:43.420 --> 00:36:45.462
We've only really
had time to get Splinter...

484
00:36:45.501 --> 00:36:47.460
- And pick up a few essentials.
- Yeah!

485
00:36:47.541 --> 00:36:49.903
The bare essentials!

486
00:36:49.981 --> 00:36:52.902
Look. the reason why
we're calling is...

487
00:36:52.981 --> 00:36:55.781
have you seen Raphael
by any chance?

488
00:36:55.861 --> 00:36:57.701
Yeah. Has he stopped by
or anything?

489
00:36:57.782 --> 00:37:01.143
No. Why? Is he missing?

490
00:37:01.220 --> 00:37:05.622
You know. there's still more stuff
to help with. Michaelangelo!

491
00:37:05.661 --> 00:37:08.062
Hey. i'm helping Donny!
Give me the phone.

492
00:37:08.102 --> 00:37:10.581
Hey. give me that...

493
00:37:10.622 --> 00:37:13.782
- So you haven't seen him at all?
- No. I haven't.

494
00:37:13.822 --> 00:37:17.021
if she does. tell him thanks
for wasting our time!

495
00:37:17.062 --> 00:37:19.263
'Cause instead of looking
for the Foot and the ooze...

496
00:37:19.343 --> 00:37:21.181
like we should...

497
00:37:21.262 --> 00:37:25.023
we gotta go out and look
for him instead.

498
00:37:25.063 --> 00:37:30.302
- What was that?
- Leo says hi.

499
00:37:30.342 --> 00:37:32.222
- Donny. give me the phone.
- If you do hear something...

500
00:37:32.302 --> 00:37:35.502
- Let us know.
- I wanna talk to April! It's important!

501
00:37:35.583 --> 00:37:37.662
- Gimme. gimme. gimme!
- All right. here.

502
00:37:37.743 --> 00:37:40.863
April. it's Mikey.
i'd just like to say...

503
00:37:40.944 --> 00:37:43.863
- Hello.
- Would you give me that!

504
00:37:49.583 --> 00:37:52.183
The cells will
no longer hold them.

505
00:37:53.342 --> 00:37:56.064
Remove the bar.

506
00:37:56.105 --> 00:37:58.583
it's time they learn
who their master is.

507
00:38:00.464 --> 00:38:03.823
Remove the bar
and leave us.

508
00:38:11.265 --> 00:38:13.584
Come forth!

509
00:38:23.105 --> 00:38:27.665
Wolf. Snapping turtle.
incredible!

510
00:38:28.305 --> 00:38:30.424
Yes. Come forward.

511
00:38:30.465 --> 00:38:33.183
Attack me. if you will.

512
00:38:33.224 --> 00:38:36.584
When it is over.
you will call me "Master"!

513
00:38:45.745 --> 00:38:49.145
- Mama? Oh. Mama!
- Oh. Mama!

514
00:38:51.264 --> 00:38:54.585
- Mama.
- Mama.

515
00:38:54.624 --> 00:38:56.825
Get off me!

516
00:38:58.745 --> 00:39:00.825
Babies!

517
00:39:00.905 --> 00:39:03.545
They are babies!

518
00:39:06.146 --> 00:39:09.146
What did you expect?
They'd come out quoting Macbeth?

519
00:39:09.226 --> 00:39:13.026
- They are stupid!
- They're not stupid. They're infants.

520
00:39:16.546 --> 00:39:18.306
Okay. they're stupid infants.

521
00:39:21.266 --> 00:39:23.386
Put that down!

522
00:39:25.466 --> 00:39:29.546
Fortunately. they seem to have
imprinted you as their surrogate mother.

523
00:39:29.625 --> 00:39:33.347
- Mama.
- They are of no use to me against a...

524
00:39:35.267 --> 00:39:37.266
See that these two things...

525
00:39:37.345 --> 00:39:40.426
are properly disposed of.

526
00:39:40.506 --> 00:39:42.427
No. You can't do that.
They're living creatures.

527
00:39:43.746 --> 00:39:45.587
Not for long.

528
00:39:45.667 --> 00:39:48.746
Hey. no. no.
Wait. look.

529
00:39:50.187 --> 00:39:54.267
They may be
intellectually inferior. but...

530
00:39:58.346 --> 00:40:01.987
As you can see. they do have
other attributes.

531
00:40:05.547 --> 00:40:09.227
Maybe i'll keep them
around after all.

532
00:40:18.666 --> 00:40:21.188
- Hey. man. how's it going?
- Pretty good.

533
00:40:21.267 --> 00:40:23.346
- Good to see you. man.
- What's up?

534
00:40:23.426 --> 00:40:25.268
Did you just get here?

535
00:40:26.467 --> 00:40:28.587
Okay. guys.

536
00:40:28.668 --> 00:40:30.827
Listen up.

537
00:40:30.908 --> 00:40:33.507
i'm only going
to tell youse once.

538
00:40:33.587 --> 00:40:37.948
All of youse guys is gonna
have to take a little test.

539
00:40:37.989 --> 00:40:41.148
Then. if you're good enough...

540
00:40:41.188 --> 00:40:44.588
we let you into
the organization.

541
00:40:44.668 --> 00:40:47.909
Any questions?

542
00:40:47.989 --> 00:40:49.469
Okay. follow me.

543
00:40:49.509 --> 00:40:51.628
- Let's go.
- Lead the way. man.

544
00:41:02.508 --> 00:41:04.028
i knew this would work.

545
00:41:04.109 --> 00:41:07.669
just remember. we get you in.
we find the Foot headquarters...

546
00:41:07.748 --> 00:41:10.148
we get you out to tell
the others. right?

547
00:41:10.229 --> 00:41:12.710
Gee. maybe i should
write this down.

548
00:41:12.789 --> 00:41:14.829
What?

549
00:41:14.909 --> 00:41:16.990
i'm being punished. aren't i?

550
00:42:02.190 --> 00:42:04.431
- Keno. wasn't it?
- Yeah.

551
00:42:04.511 --> 00:42:07.110
You seem to be the only one
worthy of a final test.

552
00:42:09.231 --> 00:42:12.472
You'll have 15 seconds to remove
as many of the bells as you can.

553
00:42:13.350 --> 00:42:15.231
One sound and you fail.

554
00:42:15.271 --> 00:42:18.511
And another thing.
we work in concealment.

555
00:42:18.592 --> 00:42:20.471
Fifteen seconds.

556
00:42:20.552 --> 00:42:21.711
Go!

557
00:42:38.152 --> 00:42:39.232
is this enough?

558
00:42:41.831 --> 00:42:44.071
Yeah!

559
00:42:46.952 --> 00:42:48.793
Welcome to our headquarters.

560
00:42:50.671 --> 00:42:53.593
Get yourself a training dogi
and meet me back in the yard.

561
00:42:53.671 --> 00:42:55.113
Yeah. right.

562
00:43:05.351 --> 00:43:06.793
Keno. come on.

563
00:43:10.632 --> 00:43:13.473
Okay. Looks like
this is the place.

564
00:43:13.553 --> 00:43:15.433
Yeah. looks like it.

565
00:43:19.553 --> 00:43:22.594
First chance we get.
we're out of here.

566
00:43:22.673 --> 00:43:24.673
What? What is it?

567
00:43:26.832 --> 00:43:28.873
i thought i just saw a ghost.

568
00:43:30.433 --> 00:43:31.633
Come on.

569
00:43:32.553 --> 00:43:36.034
- What are we looking for anyway?
- Quiet. You want to get us...

570
00:43:38.233 --> 00:43:39.712
caught?

571
00:43:39.793 --> 00:43:40.793
Yeah. well...

572
00:43:42.193 --> 00:43:46.193
Hi. We were lookin' for
a muffler for a '77 Chevy.

573
00:43:49.193 --> 00:43:51.835
Whatever happened
to service with a smile?

574
00:43:54.274 --> 00:43:55.393
Yeah!

575
00:44:00.074 --> 00:44:03.754
Get out of here kid.
Go tell the others. Go now!

576
00:44:03.793 --> 00:44:06.154
Hey. nice shot.

577
00:44:06.234 --> 00:44:08.074
You're good.
Come on.

578
00:44:10.914 --> 00:44:13.315
- I'm not gonna just...
- Run. or i'll kick your butt.

579
00:44:17.435 --> 00:44:19.875
Move!
Come on. you guys!

580
00:44:26.795 --> 00:44:29.516
Excuse me.
Pardon me.

581
00:44:32.393 --> 00:44:34.994
Come on.

582
00:44:35.075 --> 00:44:36.395
Missed.

583
00:44:38.355 --> 00:44:40.235
i'm curious.

584
00:44:40.276 --> 00:44:44.395
Any of you guys ever heard
the expression "fair fight"?

585
00:44:46.795 --> 00:44:49.235
You know. pal.
if i had a face like yours...

586
00:44:49.316 --> 00:44:52.596
i'd try to make up for it
with some sort of a personality.

587
00:45:11.116 --> 00:45:15.398
Come on.
Come on. April. Leo!

588
00:45:15.437 --> 00:45:17.516
if you're there.
it's me. Keno.

589
00:45:17.596 --> 00:45:21.517
Darn. Come on.
Raph's in trouble.

590
00:45:24.357 --> 00:45:25.956
April. where are they?

591
00:45:26.036 --> 00:45:28.636
- It's Raph.
- Wait. calm down. What happened?

592
00:45:28.716 --> 00:45:30.757
i've gotta tell the guys.
They got him!

593
00:45:30.836 --> 00:45:32.717
Who has got him?

594
00:45:42.477 --> 00:45:44.318
Come on.

595
00:45:45.356 --> 00:45:48.118
- Just like Keno said.
- Yeah.

596
00:45:48.196 --> 00:45:50.358
- The perimeter's quiet.
- Yeah.

597
00:45:50.438 --> 00:45:52.956
A little too quiet.

598
00:45:53.037 --> 00:45:55.558
- Come on.
- Okay.

599
00:46:07.918 --> 00:46:09.399
Knock. knock.

600
00:46:13.076 --> 00:46:16.358
- Well. that was easy.
- Yeah. a little too easy.

601
00:46:21.997 --> 00:46:24.317
Look. it's Raph!

602
00:46:24.398 --> 00:46:26.519
Yeah. a little too Raph.

603
00:46:26.597 --> 00:46:30.198
You guys. knock it off.
Keep your eyes peeled.

604
00:46:30.278 --> 00:46:32.199
i don't like this.

605
00:46:32.278 --> 00:46:33.478
- Let's go.
- Right.

606
00:46:46.438 --> 00:46:48.999
You know. given the layout
of this junkyard...

607
00:46:49.039 --> 00:46:51.079
and the proximity
of certain structures...

608
00:46:51.118 --> 00:46:53.039
if they were gonna
spring a trap...

609
00:46:53.079 --> 00:46:56.039
they'd probably do it
right about...

610
00:46:59.958 --> 00:47:01.959
Let us out of here!

611
00:47:02.039 --> 00:47:03.799
What the...

612
00:47:08.279 --> 00:47:10.759
The Shred dude!
it's him!

613
00:47:10.839 --> 00:47:14.159
i've been waiting for you.

614
00:47:14.200 --> 00:47:16.839
i have a little surprise.

615
00:47:18.360 --> 00:47:22.760
- Oh. no.
- I don't like this.

616
00:47:22.840 --> 00:47:24.718
i wonder what those are for.

617
00:47:24.759 --> 00:47:27.640
Does the word "turtle-kabob"
mean anything to you?

618
00:47:27.720 --> 00:47:31.201
Yeah. right!
Get your arm out of my face.

619
00:47:34.400 --> 00:47:37.720
Patience.
First them...

620
00:47:37.800 --> 00:47:41.161
then you.

621
00:47:41.241 --> 00:47:44.120
You know. these nets
are remarkably effective.

622
00:47:44.200 --> 00:47:46.040
Very well constructed.

623
00:47:46.120 --> 00:47:49.160
Remind me to drop a line
to Ralph Nader!

624
00:47:49.201 --> 00:47:52.521
Wait for my signal
to drop them.

625
00:47:55.120 --> 00:47:57.041
i never got to see Paris.

626
00:47:57.081 --> 00:47:59.961
A little closer.

627
00:48:00.040 --> 00:48:02.281
A little closer!

628
00:48:02.321 --> 00:48:04.802
Oh. we're almost there!

629
00:48:06.322 --> 00:48:07.762
Get ready!

630
00:48:14.361 --> 00:48:17.322
Cowabunga!

631
00:48:17.401 --> 00:48:19.840
That's right. Shredder.
You forgot.

632
00:48:19.920 --> 00:48:23.882
- We carry insurance.
- Mutual of Splinter. dude.

633
00:48:23.922 --> 00:48:25.921
Get them!

634
00:48:39.761 --> 00:48:41.883
Why don't you just
rip my lips off?

635
00:48:41.962 --> 00:48:44.802
- You'd think...
- Enough.

636
00:48:44.883 --> 00:48:46.922
Here. let me get this first.

637
00:48:58.683 --> 00:49:01.162
Can we talk?

638
00:49:01.204 --> 00:49:02.482
Guess not!

639
00:49:04.804 --> 00:49:06.883
Pitiful.

640
00:49:15.403 --> 00:49:16.523
You win.

641
00:49:19.844 --> 00:49:22.564
- Looks like we're on our own.
- All right!

642
00:49:22.644 --> 00:49:24.683
Tokka!

643
00:49:24.723 --> 00:49:26.963
Rahzar!

644
00:49:37.964 --> 00:49:40.164
Didn't we see these guys
on Wrestlemania?

645
00:49:40.245 --> 00:49:43.924
Prove yourselves to me!
Attack!

646
00:49:46.044 --> 00:49:48.325
Well. you know
what they say.

647
00:49:48.403 --> 00:49:50.245
The bigger they are...

648
00:49:53.765 --> 00:49:55.324
The more bones
they break.

649
00:49:58.805 --> 00:50:01.764
- These guys are mine.
- Go get 'em. Donny.

650
00:50:01.845 --> 00:50:05.446
All right. you overgrown.
ugly excuse for a turtle!

651
00:50:11.283 --> 00:50:15.684
You know. maybe that "ugly" crack
was a little bit out of line.

652
00:50:23.886 --> 00:50:26.286
Oh. that hurt!

653
00:50:29.005 --> 00:50:31.485
Hey. you're that TGRi guy.

654
00:50:31.566 --> 00:50:33.405
Hang on.

655
00:50:35.525 --> 00:50:39.765
- I've got to get the hang of that.
- It's okay.

656
00:50:39.845 --> 00:50:42.326
i'm gonna get you
out of here.

657
00:50:58.445 --> 00:50:59.566
What?

658
00:51:01.806 --> 00:51:03.887
Oh. am i glad to see you!

659
00:51:06.527 --> 00:51:10.446
- Hey. guys. over here!
- Yeah! We're on our way.

660
00:51:11.927 --> 00:51:15.206
Come on. Professor.
We don't have a lot of time.

661
00:51:15.286 --> 00:51:19.847
- Hey. Mikey. we got the TGRi guy.
- Come on. come on.

662
00:51:19.926 --> 00:51:23.247
- Well. actually. i'd rather not.
- Come on!

663
00:51:25.047 --> 00:51:27.566
Step up to the bar. boys!

664
00:51:31.328 --> 00:51:33.206
This way. Leo.
Come on.

665
00:51:34.047 --> 00:51:35.568
You all right. Doc?

666
00:51:35.608 --> 00:51:38.807
- Way to go. Mikey!
- Come on. You go next.

667
00:51:38.848 --> 00:51:40.288
Come here.

668
00:51:41.367 --> 00:51:43.607
- Come on. Raph.
- Yeah. yeah.

669
00:51:45.168 --> 00:51:46.288
Stop them!

670
00:51:51.007 --> 00:51:54.248
- Drop right in. Leo.
- All right!

671
00:52:07.128 --> 00:52:09.968
Hey. look at this!

672
00:52:19.768 --> 00:52:20.768
Stupid!

673
00:52:23.129 --> 00:52:25.769
Come on. We gotta
meet back up with Splinter.

674
00:52:25.849 --> 00:52:27.369
Yeah.

675
00:52:30.209 --> 00:52:33.369
Four walking. talking turtles!

676
00:52:36.168 --> 00:52:39.249
Yeah. the guy's Ph.D. material.
all right.

677
00:52:39.289 --> 00:52:42.129
You're so intelligent.
it's incredible.

678
00:52:42.169 --> 00:52:45.568
Don't freak. dude.
We can explain. You see...

679
00:52:45.649 --> 00:52:47.689
Fifteen years ago.
you came into contact...

680
00:52:47.770 --> 00:52:49.969
with a green colloidal gel
down in a sewer...

681
00:52:50.009 --> 00:52:53.409
which transformed you
into your present state.

682
00:52:54.489 --> 00:52:55.888
Fantastic!

683
00:52:56.449 --> 00:52:59.249
There you go.
Come on. Yeah.

684
00:52:59.289 --> 00:53:00.810
Amazing. guys.

685
00:53:00.889 --> 00:53:04.370
i thought all the really
good dungeons were in Europe.

686
00:53:04.451 --> 00:53:06.169
There you go. dude.

687
00:53:09.290 --> 00:53:11.892
- This is wonderful!
- Yeah. okay.

688
00:53:11.930 --> 00:53:15.889
We'll give you the tour later.
Right now we've got a few questions.

689
00:53:15.930 --> 00:53:20.291
- A few inquiries.
- Yeah. a few...

690
00:53:20.371 --> 00:53:23.729
- We'll give you a tour later.
- Give him room to speak.

691
00:53:26.010 --> 00:53:29.011
The professor has much
to tell us.

692
00:53:36.571 --> 00:53:38.531
Of course. laboratories
were crude back then...

693
00:53:38.612 --> 00:53:41.610
and an accident was
just waiting to happen.

694
00:53:41.690 --> 00:53:45.051
Wait a minute.
You mean to tell us...

695
00:53:45.131 --> 00:53:48.812
that the formation of the ooze
was all just a big mistake?

696
00:53:48.891 --> 00:53:50.851
Let me see.

697
00:53:50.931 --> 00:53:53.492
Donatello. isn't it?

698
00:53:53.532 --> 00:53:56.092
An unknown mixture
of discarded chemicals...

699
00:53:56.172 --> 00:53:59.850
was accidentally exposed
to a series of radiated waves...

700
00:53:59.931 --> 00:54:03.211
and the resulting ooze
was found to have remarkable...

701
00:54:03.291 --> 00:54:06.733
but dangerous
mutanagenic properties.

702
00:54:08.571 --> 00:54:09.851
Big mistake.

703
00:54:14.132 --> 00:54:17.412
- Please continue. Professor.
- Yeah.

704
00:54:17.492 --> 00:54:20.052
Well. on our way to bury them.
a near collision caused us...

705
00:54:20.091 --> 00:54:24.492
to lose one of the canisters
down a sewer 15 years ago.

706
00:54:24.572 --> 00:54:28.052
Professor Perry.
what's happening at TGRi now?

707
00:54:28.972 --> 00:54:30.892
i imagine they're trying
to remove any evidence...

708
00:54:30.972 --> 00:54:33.413
of the disposal process
and evacuate the premises...

709
00:54:33.493 --> 00:54:36.372
which is standard procedure
when a mishap occurs.

710
00:54:36.413 --> 00:54:41.774
And as we know. one or two
rather big mishaps have occurred.

711
00:54:41.853 --> 00:54:45.133
Yeah.
Tokka. Rahzar and the Shredder.

712
00:54:45.212 --> 00:54:48.492
And he's obsessed
with destroying you all.

713
00:54:48.573 --> 00:54:51.493
Yeah. we got that impression.
all right.

714
00:54:51.574 --> 00:54:52.933
- Michaelangelo.
- Yeah?

715
00:54:53.014 --> 00:54:55.372
- Show the professor where he may rest.
- Righty-o!

716
00:54:56.374 --> 00:54:58.092
This way. dude.

717
00:54:58.173 --> 00:55:06.053
it ain't the Hilton. Let's face it. You'd
be better off staying at the Hilton.

718
00:55:12.613 --> 00:55:16.654
What troubles you. my son?

719
00:55:16.733 --> 00:55:20.853
i don't know. I just always thought
there'd be more to it...

720
00:55:20.893 --> 00:55:22.852
to the ooze...

721
00:55:22.934 --> 00:55:26.095
to. you know. us!

722
00:55:26.175 --> 00:55:28.134
i know.

723
00:55:28.214 --> 00:55:34.414
i always thought
there'd be something. i thought we'd
find out we were special.

724
00:55:35.135 --> 00:55:39.213
Do not confuse the specter
of your origin...

725
00:55:39.294 --> 00:55:41.575
with your present worth.
my sons.

726
00:55:41.654 --> 00:55:45.935
i don't believe him!
There's just got to be more to it!

727
00:55:46.016 --> 00:55:48.694
Perhaps the search
for a beginning...

728
00:55:48.734 --> 00:55:52.656
rarely has so easy an end.

729
00:55:52.734 --> 00:55:55.816
But our search
will have to wait.

730
00:55:55.895 --> 00:55:59.695
Tonight's encounter
has left us with...

731
00:55:59.776 --> 00:56:02.215
larger problems.

732
00:56:06.216 --> 00:56:07.134
i got 'em.

733
00:56:15.216 --> 00:56:19.056
Go. Play. Have fun.

734
00:56:19.134 --> 00:56:20.976
Fun!

735
00:56:24.456 --> 00:56:28.055
Tonight we leave a calling card
for the turtles.

736
00:56:28.095 --> 00:56:32.816
Tomorrow we force
a final confrontation.

737
00:56:58.177 --> 00:57:01.817
- Master say have fun!
- Fun!

738
00:57:03.457 --> 00:57:05.297
Look. Sophie.

739
00:57:05.377 --> 00:57:07.817
Some animals are knocking down
the telephone poles.

740
00:57:07.897 --> 00:57:09.977
What do we do
if they come over here?

741
00:57:10.018 --> 00:57:12.496
Let them get
their own cab.

742
00:57:24.418 --> 00:57:26.258
Damage is minimal.

743
00:57:26.337 --> 00:57:29.616
And as always. our official report
will be released...

744
00:57:29.698 --> 00:57:31.538
after a thorough investigation.

745
00:57:31.618 --> 00:57:33.458
Thank you. Miss O'Neil.

746
00:57:33.538 --> 00:57:36.338
i have no further comments
at this time.

747
00:57:36.418 --> 00:57:38.258
We will be in touch.

748
00:57:38.337 --> 00:57:41.657
More as it develops.
Here you go.

749
00:57:41.697 --> 00:57:44.579
Chief Sterns. i wonder
if i might ask you...

750
00:57:44.618 --> 00:57:46.779
a few more questions
off-the-record.

751
00:57:46.818 --> 00:57:48.777
Miss O'Neil. my record.
on-the-record...

752
00:57:48.858 --> 00:57:51.898
clearly shows that i have
